Spam Classification Using Machine Learning

# 1. Developed an end-to-end spam classification system to distinguish between spam and ham messages.
# 2. Utilized text preprocessing techniques, including tokenization, stemming, and stopword removal, for cleaning and transforming the text data.
# 3. Extracted features using TF-IDF vectorization and numerical attributes such as character and word counts.
# 4. Implemented and compared multiple classifiers (Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, Random Forest) and advanced ensemble methods (Voting, Stacking Classifiers).
# 5. Visualized performance metrics and key insights using Python libraries like Matplotlib and Seaborn.
# 6. Optimized the model to achieve a high precision score, ensuring minimal false positives in spam detection.
